Obsoletes:      texlive-combelow-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-combelow
The package defines a command \cb that positions a comma below a letter, as
required (for example) in Romanian typesetting. The command is robust, but
interferes with hyphenation.

%package -n texlive-combine
Summary:        Bundle individual documents into a single document
Version:        svn19361
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-combine-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-combine-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-combine
The combine class lets you bundle individual documents into a single document,
such as when preparing a conference proceedings. The auxiliary combinet package
puts the titles and authors from \maketitle commands into the main document's
Table of Contents. The package cooperates with the abstract and titling
packages.

%package -n texlive-comma
Summary:        Formats a number by inserting commas
Version:        svn78931
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
