Provides:       texlive-comma-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-comma-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-comma
A flexible package that allows commas (or anything else) to be inserted every
three digits in a number, as in 1,234.

%package -n texlive-commado
Summary:        Expandable iteration on comma-separated and filename lists
Version:        svn38875
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-commado-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-commado-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-commado
The bundle provides two packages: commado and filesdo. The package commado
provides the command \DoWithCSL: \DoWithCSL{<cmd>}{<list>} applies an existing
one-parameter macro <cmd> to each item in a list <list> in which terms are
separated by commas. The package filesdo provides the command \DoWithBasesExts:
\DoWithBasesExts{<cmd>}{<bases>}{<exts>} which runs the single parameter
command <cmd> on each file whose base and extension are respectively from the
comma-separated lists <bases> and <exts>. These 'loop'-like commands are
(themselves) entirely expandable. The packages rely on packages plainpkg, and
stacklet

%package -n texlive-commalists-tools
Summary:        Manipulate numeral comma separated lists
Version:        svn78486
License:        LPPL-1.3c
