\section, etc. The documentation shows a number of document-management
scenarios in which such commands are valuable.

%package -n texlive-count1to
Summary:        Make use of count1 to count9
Version:        svn71526
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(everyshi.sty)

%description -n texlive-count1to
A LaTeX package which sets count 1 (to 'absolute' page number), counts 2-8 to
the numbers of the current \part, \chapter (always 0 in article class), ...
\subparagraph, and count 9 to 1 or 0, according to whether the page is odd or
even. These values can be used to select pages with some drivers. The package
uses the everyshi package.

%package -n texlive-counterz
Summary:        Additional tools for counters
Version:        svn67335
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(makecmds.sty)

%description -n texlive-counterz
The package facilitates the use of stealth prefixes for counter names in order
to help distinguish between counters from multiple input files. The package
also provides a means to generate random counters and save such counter values
for future typesetting.

%package -n texlive-counttexruns
Summary:        Count compilations of a document
Version:        svn27576
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
