%description -n texlive-diabetes-logbook
Initially a logbook for me, a person with type one diabetes mellitus, this
evolved over time into a TeX project, making it prettier and/or easier to use.
I've made it simple to use, while not forgoing the document's beauty or the
speed of input. The logbook, with slight commenting out and editing, could be
used as a journal by anybody, although the template and graphing functionality
are set up for people using insulin injections and blood glucose teststrips, as
well as counting/estimating carbs, protein, and fat. Note: The names of the
package's files are not constructed using the long "diabetes-logbook", but the
acronym "dmlb" (for "diabetes mellitus log book").

%package -n texlive-diagbox
Summary:        Table heads with diagonal lines
Version:        svn77682
