%description -n texlive-diagbox
The package's principal command, \diagbox, takes two arguments (texts for the
slash-separated parts of the box), and an optional argument with which the
direction the slash will go, the box dimensions, etc., may be controlled. The
package also provides \slashbox and \backslashbox commands for compatibility
with the slashbox package, which it supersedes. diagbox depends on e-TeX as
well as the packages array, calc, fp, keyval, and pict2e.

