Implements a document layout for writing letters according to the rules of DIN
(Deutsches Institut fur Normung, German standardisation institute). A style
file for LaTeX 2.09 (with limited support of the features) is part of the
package. Since the letter layout is based on a German standard, the user guide
is written in German, but most macros have English names from which the user
can recognize what they are used for. In addition there are example files
showing how letters may be created with the package. A graphical interface for
use of the dinbrief is provided in the dinbrief-GUI bundle.

