%description -n texlive-doi
You can hyperlink DOI numbers to doi.org. However, some publishers have elected
to use nasty characters in their DOI numbering scheme ('<', '>', '_' and ';'
have all been spotted). This will either upset (La)TeX, or your PDF reader.
This package contains a single user-level command \doi{}, which takes a DOI
number, and creates a correct hyperlink to the target of the DOI.

