The package simplifies the indexing of words using the \index command of
makeidx. With the package, to index a word in a text, you only have to type it
once; the package makes sure it is both typeset and indexed.

%package -n texlive-hvlogos
Summary:        Print TeX-related names as logo
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(dantelogo.sty)
Requires:       tex(fetamont.sty)
Requires:       tex(hologo.sty)
Requires:       tex(tikz.sty)
Requires:       tex(unicode-math.sty)
Requires:       tex(xspace.sty)

%description -n texlive-hvlogos
This package is more or less an extension to Heiko Oberdiek's package hologo.
It prints TeX-related names as logos. The package requires fetamont, hologo,
dantelogo, and xspace.

%package -n texlive-hvpygmentex
Summary:        Syntax-Highlighting of program code
Version:        svn62405
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(caption.sty)
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
