Requires:       tex(iftex.sty)
Requires:       tex(pdfescape.sty)
Requires:       tex(pdftexcmds.sty)

%description -n texlive-hypdestopt
This package supports hyperref's pdfTeX driver. It removes unnecessary
destinations and shortens the destination names or uses numbered destinations
to get smaller PDF files.

%package -n texlive-hypdoc
Summary:        Hyper extensions for doc.sty
Version:        svn68661
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(atveryend.sty)
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(doc.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(rerunfilecheck.sty)

%description -n texlive-hypdoc
This package adds hypertext features to the package doc that is used in the
documentation system of LaTeX2e. Bookmarks are added and references are linked
as far as possible.

%package -n texlive-hypdvips
Summary:        Hyperref extensions for use with dvips
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-hypdvips-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-hypdvips-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(atveryend.sty)
Requires:       tex(bookmark.sty)
Requires:       tex(hypcap.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-hypdvips
The hypdvips package fixes some problems when using hyperref with dvips. It
also adds support for breaking links, file attachments, embedded documents and
different types of GoTo-links. The cooperation of hyperref with cleveref is
improved, which in addition allows an enhanced back-referencing system.

%package -n texlive-hyper
Summary:        Hypertext cross referencing
Version:        svn17357
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-hyper-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-hyper-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
Requires:       tex(defpattern.sty)

%description -n texlive-hyper
Redefines LaTeX cross-referencing commands to insert \special commands for
HyperTeX dvi viewers, such as recent versions of xdvi. The package is now
largely superseded by hyperref.

%package -n texlive-hyperbar
Summary:        Add interactive Barcode fields to PDF forms
Version:        svn48147
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)

%description -n texlive-hyperbar
The package extends the hyperref functionality for creating interactive forms
to allow adding Barcode form fields supported by some modern PDF readers.
Currently, only pdfTeX is supported.

%package -n texlive-hypernat
Summary:        Allow hyperref and natbib to work together
Version:        svn17358
License:        GPL-2.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-hypernat-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-hypernat-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-hypernat
Allows hyperref package and the natbib package with options 'numbers' and
'sort&compress' to work together. This means that multiple sequential citations
(e.g [3,2,1]) will be compressed to [1-3], where the '1' and the '3' are
(color-)linked to the bibliography.

%package -n texlive-hyphenat
Summary:        Disable/enable hyphenation
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-hyphenat-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-hyphenat-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-hyphenat
This package can disable all hyphenation or enable hyphenation of
non-alphabetics or monospaced fonts. The package can also enable hyphenation
within 'words' that contain non-alphabetic characters (e.g., that include
underscores), and hyphenation of text typeset in monospaced (e.g., cmtt) fonts.

%package -n texlive-identkey
