Provides:       texlive-inversepath-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-inversepath-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-inversepath
The package calculates inverse relative paths. Such things may be useful, for
example, when writing an auxiliary file to a different directory.

%package -n texlive-invoice
Summary:        Generate invoices
Version:        svn48359
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-invoice-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-invoice-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(fp.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(longtable.sty)
Requires:       tex(siunitx.sty)

%description -n texlive-invoice
The package may be used for generating invoices. The package can deal with
invisible expense items and deductions; output may be presented in any of 10
different languages. A long-standing bug has been removed. Numbers now can show
the comma as decimal separator. The package depends on the fp, calc and siunitx
for its calculations.

%package -n texlive-invoice-class
Summary:        Produces a standard US invoice from a CSV file
Version:        svn49749
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-invoice-class
This class produces a standard US commercial invoice using data from a CSV
file. Invoices can span multiple pages. The class is configurable for different
shipping addresses.

%package -n texlive-invoice2
Summary:        Intelligent invoices with LaTeX3
Version:        svn67327
License:        GPL-3.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       texlive-booktabs
Requires:       texlive-l3kernel
Requires:       texlive-l3packages
Requires:       texlive-siunitx
