Provides:       texlive-linegoal-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-linegoal-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(etex.sty)
Requires:       tex(zref-savepos.sty)
Requires:       tex(zref.sty)

%description -n texlive-linegoal
The linegoal package provides a macro \linegoal to be used with \setlength:
\setlength<some dimen>\linegoal will set <some dimen> to the horizontal length
of the remainder of the line. This is achieved using the \pdfsavepos primitive
of pdfTeX, through the zref-savepos package. Example: Some text:
\begin{tabularx}\linegoal{|l|X|} \hline one & two \\ three & four \\\hline
\end{tabularx} will position the table after the initial text, and make the
table fill the rest of the line.

