any browser to view the result. Can be used to replace \tl_analysis_show:n.

%package -n texlive-printlen
Summary:        Print lengths using specified units
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-printlen-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-printlen-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-printlen
\printlength{length} prints the value of a LaTeX length in the units specified
by \uselengthunit{unit} ('unit' may be any TeX length unit except for scaled
point, viz., any of: pt, pc, in, mm, cm, bp, dd or cc). When the unit is pt,
the printed length value will include any stretch or shrink; otherwise these
are not printed. The 'unit' argument may also be PT, in which case length
values will be printed in point units but without any stretch or shrink values.

%package -n texlive-probsoln
Summary:        Generate problem sheets and their solution sheets
Version:        svn44783
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-probsoln-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
