This package combines several other packages and defines additional macros and
environments for documenting LaTeX code. The package mainly serves the purpose
of combining the preferences used in the author's own package documentations.
However, others can use the package as well. Compatibility between versions
cannot be guaranteed, however.

%package -n texlive-rjlparshap
Summary:        Support for use of \parshape in LaTeX
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-rjlparshap-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-rjlparshap-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(arrayjob.sty)
Requires:       tex(forloop.sty)

%description -n texlive-rjlparshap
The package provides macros and environments that relieve the programmer of
some of the difficulties of using \parshape in LaTeX macros. It does not
actually calculate shapes in the way that the shapepar package does.

%package -n texlive-rlepsf
Summary:        Rewrite labels in EPS graphics
Version:        svn19082
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-rlepsf-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-rlepsf-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-rlepsf
A macro package for use with epsf.tex which allows PostScript labels in an
Encapsulated PostScript file to be replaced by TeX labels. The package provides
commands \relabel (simply replace a PostScript string), \adjustrelabel (replace
a PostScript string, with position adjustment), and \extralabel (add a label at
given coordinates). You can, if you so choose, use the facilities of the
labelfig package in place of using \extralabel.

%package -n texlive-rmpage
Summary:        A package to help change page layout parameters in LaTeX
Version:        svn54080
License:        GPL-2.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-rmpage-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-rmpage-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(avant.sty)
Requires:       tex(beton.sty)
Requires:       tex(bookman.sty)
Requires:       tex(chancery.sty)
Requires:       tex(helvet.sty)
# Ignoring dependency on lucasual.sty - non-free
# Ignoring dependency on lucida-helvetica.sty - not part of TeX Live
Requires:       tex(newcent.sty)
Requires:       tex(palatino.sty)
Requires:       tex(times.sty)
Requires:       tex(utopia.sty)

%description -n texlive-rmpage
The package lets you change page layout parameters in small steps over a range
of values using options. It can set \textwidth appropriately for the main
fount, and ensure that the text fits inside the printable area of a printer. An
rmpage-formatted document can be typeset identically without rmpage after a
single cut and paste operation. Local configuration can set defaults: for all
documents; and by class, by printer, and by paper size. The geometry package is
better if you want to set page layout parameters to particular measurements.

%package -n texlive-robust-externalize
Summary:        Cache anything (TikZ, python, ...) in a robust, efficient and pure way
Version:        svn76924
License:        MIT
