Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-tdclock
A ticking digital clock package to be used in Pdf-LaTeX documents, for example
in presentations.

%package -n texlive-technics
Summary:        A package to format technical documents
Version:        svn29349
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-technics-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-technics-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(fancyhdr.sty)
Requires:       tex(fontenc.sty)
Requires:       tex(graphics.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(inputenc.sty)
Requires:       tex(multicol.sty)
Requires:       tex(setspace.sty)
Requires:       tex(times.sty)

%description -n texlive-technics
The package provides a very simple LaTeX document template, in the hope that
this use of LaTeX will become attractive to typical word processor users.
(Presentation is as if it were a class; users are expected to start from a
template document.)

%package -n texlive-ted
Summary:        A (primitive) token list editor
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-ted-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-ted-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-ted
Just like sed is a stream editor, ted is a token list editor. Actually, it is
not as powerful as sed, but its main feature is that it really works with
tokens, not only characters. The ted package provides two user macros:
\Substitute and \ShowTokens. The first is maybe the most useful: it performs
substitutions in token lists (even inside braces). The second displays each
token of the list (one per line) with its catcode (in the list, not just the
current one), and can be useful for debugging or for TeX learners. Ted is
designed to work well even if strange tokens (that is, unusual {charcode,
catcode} pairs or tokens with a confusing meaning) occur in the list.

%package -n texlive-telprint
Summary:        Format German phone numbers
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-telprint
The package provides a command \telprint for formatting German telephone
numbers.

%package -n texlive-templatetools
Summary:        Commands useful in LaTeX templates
Version:        svn67201
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-templatetools-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-templatetools-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(array.sty)
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifdraft.sty)
Requires:       tex(iftex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ltxcmds.sty)
Requires:       tex(scrlfile.sty)

%description -n texlive-templatetools
The package provides a collection of tools, which are helpful for the creation
of a LaTeX template if conditional paths for code execution are required. All
the commands work both in the preamble and in the document.

%package -n texlive-termcal
Summary:        Print a class calendar
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-termcal-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-termcal-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(longtable.sty)

%description -n texlive-termcal
This package is intended to print a term calendar for use in planning a class.
It has a flexible mechanism for specifying which days of the week are to be
included and for inserting text either regularly on the same day each week, or
on selected days, or for a series of consecutive days. It also has a flexible
mechanism for specifying class and nonclass days. Text may be inserted into
consecutive days so that it automatically flows around nonclass days.

%package -n texlive-terminalcode
Summary:        Terminal-style code display with ANSI colors, UTF-8 box-drawing, and dark/light themes
Version:        svn76729
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(ctex.sty)
Requires:       tex(fontspec.sty)
Requires:       tex(kvoptions.sty)
Requires:       tex(listings.sty)
Requires:       tex(tcolorbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)

%description -n texlive-terminalcode
The terminalcode package provides authentic terminal-style code display
environments for LaTeX documents. It features UTF-8 box-drawing characters,
comprehensive ANSI 16-color support with dynamic dark and light themes, and
seamless integration with external code files. Requires LuaLaTeX or XeLaTeX.

%package -n texlive-termlist
Summary:        Label any kind of term with a continuous counter
Version:        svn18923
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-termlist-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-termlist-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-termlist
The termlist package provides environments to indent and label any kind of
terms with a continuous number. Candidate terms may appear inside an equation
or eqnarray environment.

%package -n texlive-termsim
Summary:        Simulate Win10, Ubuntu, and Mac terminals
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-termsim
This LaTeX3 package provides environments terminal and terminal*, and macros
\termfile and \termfile* to simulate Win10, Ubuntu and Mac terminals. It is
based on tcolorbox, minted and listings.

%package -n texlive-testhyphens
Summary:        Testing hyphenation patterns
Version:        svn73486
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-testhyphens-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-testhyphens-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-testhyphens
The package may be used for testing hyphenation patterns or for controlling
that specific words are hyphenated as expected. This package implements some
old TUGboat code to adapt it to LaTeX with some enhancements. It differs form
\showhyphens, because it typesets its output on the document's output file. It
also works with xelatex, where \showhyphens requires a workaround.

%package -n texlive-testidx
Summary:        Dummy text for testing index styles and indexing applications
Version:        svn60966
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
Requires:       tex(glossary-mcols.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifluatex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifxetex.sty)

%description -n texlive-testidx
This is a LaTeX package that provides a command to produce dummy text
interspersed with \index commands to test an index style or indexing
application. The dummy text is mostly in English, but includes extended Latin
characters provided either through LaTeX accent commands or directly with UTF-8
characters, depending on the setup, to allow for testing extended Latin
alphabets. The supplementary package testidx-glossaries.sty uses the indexing
interface provided by the glossaries package.

%package -n texlive-tex-label
Summary:        Place a classification on each page of a document
Version:        svn16372
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-tex-label-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-tex-label-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
Requires:       tex(fancyhdr.sty)

%description -n texlive-tex-label
Enables the user to place a 'classification' label on each page, at the bottom
to the right of the page number

%package -n texlive-tex-locale
Summary:        Localisation support for TeX and LaTeX documents
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(CJK.sty)
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(fontenc.sty)
Requires:       tex(fontspec.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifluatex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifxetex.sty)
Requires:       tex(inputenc.sty)
Requires:       tex(pinyin.sty)
Requires:       tex(texosquery.sty)
Requires:       tex(tracklang-scripts.sty)
Requires:       tex(tracklang.sty)
Requires:       tex(xeCJK.sty)
Requires:       tex(xfor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-tex-locale
This package uses both tracklang and texosquery to look up the locale
information from the operating system and provide commands that can access
locale-dependent information, such as the currency symbol and decimal
separator. The file tex-locale.tex provides generic TeX code. The LaTeX package
tex-locale.sty can additionally load babel or polyglossia with the locale's
language setting, as well as various other packages such as fontspec
(XeLaTeX/LuaLaTeX) or fontenc + inputenc (pdfLaTeX).

%package -n texlive-texlogos
Summary:        Ready-to-use LaTeX logos
Version:        svn19083
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(amsmath.sty)
Requires:       tex(graphics.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)

%description -n texlive-texlogos
TeXlogos defines an assortment of frequently used logos not contained in base
LaTeX itself. The Metafont, MetapostAMS, BibTeX and SliTeX logos are defined,
as long as you have the appropriate CM/Logo/AMS fonts. Currency symbols Euro,
Cent, Yen, Won and Naira are defined so as not to need TS1-encoded fonts. Also
defined are the C++ logo, with the '+' signs properly positioned, and the logo
of the Vienna University Business Administration Center (BWZ).

%package -n texlive-texmate
Summary:        Comprehensive chess annotation in LaTeX
Version:        svn78101
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-texmate-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-texmate-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(amssymb.sty)
Requires:       tex(chessfss.sty)
Requires:       tex(skak.sty)

%description -n texlive-texmate
TeXmate formats chess games from very simple ascii input. The clean "1. e4 e5;
2. Nf3 Nc6; 3. Bb5 a6" will produce the same results as the sloppier "1 e4 e5;
Nf3 Nc6 3.. Bb5 a6". The resulting format is fully customizable. There are 4
levels of commentary: 1 is the main game, 2-3 are commentaries. Each has its
fonts, punctuation marks, etc., and these are also customizable. The package
includes a tool for the creation of diagrams. The package works in conjunction
with skak to produce diagrams of the current position automatically. For chess
fonts, the package uses the chessfss system.

%package -n texlive-texments
Summary:        Using the Pygments highlighter in LaTeX
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-texments-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-texments-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
Requires:       tex(fancyvrb.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)

%description -n texlive-texments
A package which allows to use the Pygments highlighter inside LaTeX documents.
Pygments supports syntax colouring of over 50 types of files, and ships with
multiple colour schemes.

%package -n texlive-texpower
Summary:        Create dynamic online presentations with LaTeX
Version:        svn29349
License:        GPL-2.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-texpower-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-texpower-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       texlive-tpslifonts
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
Requires:       tex(graphics.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifpdf.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(keyval.sty)
Requires:       tex(pstricks.sty)
Requires:       tex(relsize.sty)

%description -n texlive-texpower
TeXPower is a bundle of packages intended to provide an all-inclusive
environment for designing pdf screen presentations to be viewed in full-screen
mode, especially for projecting `online' with a video beamer. For some of its
core functions, it uses code derived from ppower4 packages. It is, however, not
a complete environment in itself: it relies on an existing class for preparing
slides (such as foiltex or seminar) or another package such as pdfslide.

%package -n texlive-texshade
Summary:        Package for setting nucleotide and peptide alignments
Version:        svn76586
License:        GPL-2.0-only
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-texshade-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-texshade-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(amssymb.sty)
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
Requires:       tex(graphics.sty)

%description -n texlive-texshade
TeXshade is alignment shading software completely written in TeX/LaTeX; it can
process multiple sequence alignments in the .MSF and the .ALN file formats. In
addition to common shading algorithms, it provides special shading modes
showing functional aspects, e.g. charge or hydropathy, and a wide range of
commands for handling shading colours, text styles, labels, legends; it even
allows the user to define completely new shading modes. TeXshade combines
highest flexibility with TeX output quality -- all in a bundle that does not
demand excessive development time of the user.

%package -n texlive-texsurgery
Summary:        A LaTeX companion to the "texsurgery" python project
Version:        svn59885
License:        BSD-3-Clause
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(environ.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(listings.sty)
Requires:       tex(verbatim.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)

%description -n texlive-texsurgery
This LaTeX library is a companion to the texsurgery python project. It will
make sure that "pdflatex document.tex" will work, with reasonable defaults, for
a document that is intended to work with texsurgery, and also has other uses,
always in tandem with the texsurgery pypi package.

%package -n texlive-textcsc
Summary:        Simple commands for caps-to-small-caps text
Version:        svn78632
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(fontspec.sty)
Requires:       tex(iftex.sty)

%description -n texlive-textcsc
This package provides a simple command (\textcsc and \cscshape) for
caps-to-small-caps text, to allow for small caps acronyms to be presented as
uppercase in text (useful for things like copying and pasting from a PDF).

%package -n texlive-textfit
Summary:        Fit text to a desired size
Version:        svn20591
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-textfit-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-textfit-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-textfit
Package to fit text to a given width or height by scaling the font. For
example: \scaletowidth{3in}{This}. (The job is done by calculating a magstep
and applying it to the current font; thus "This" will be very tall, as well as
very wide; to scale in just one dimension, use the facilities of the graphicx
package.)

%package -n texlive-textmerg
Summary:        Merge text in TeX and LaTeX
Version:        svn76924
License:        LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-textmerg-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-textmerg-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-textmerg
Repetitively produce documents from a fixed part and a variable part. Such an
operation is commonly used as "mail merge" to produce mail shots.

%package -n texlive-textpos
Summary:        Place boxes at arbitrary positions on the LaTeX page
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-textpos-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-textpos-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(everyshi.sty)
Requires:       tex(keyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-textpos
A package to facilitate the placement of boxes at absolute positions on the
LaTeX page. There are several reasons why this might be useful, one important
example being to help the creation of large-format conference posters.

%package -n texlive-textualicomma
Summary:        Use the textual comma character as decimal separator in math mode
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(amstext.sty)

%description -n texlive-textualicomma
The package is based on the icomma package, and intended as a solution for
situations where the text comma character discerns from the math comma
character, e.g. when fonts without math support are involved. Escaping to text
mode every time a comma is used in math mode may slow down the compilation
process.

%package -n texlive-texvc
Summary:        Use MediaWiki LaTeX commands
Version:        svn76874
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-texvc-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-texvc-doc <= 11:%{version}
