Obsoletes:      texlive-twoinone-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-twoinone
The package is for printing two pages on a single (landscape) A4 page. Page
numbers appear on the included pages, and not on the landscape 'container'
page.

%package -n texlive-twoup
Summary:        Print two virtual pages on each physical page
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-twoup-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-twoup-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-twoup
MiKTeX and many other TeX implementations include tools for massaging
PostScript into booklet and two-up printing -- that is, printing two logical
pages side by side on one side of one sheet of paper. However, some LaTeX
preliminaries are necessary to use those tools. The twoup package provides such
preliminaries and gives advice on how to use the PostScript tools.

%package -n texlive-txgreeks
Summary:        Shape selection for TX fonts Greek letters
Version:        svn21839
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-txgreeks-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-txgreeks-doc <= 11:%{version}
