%description -n texlive-unicodefonttable
This package produces font tables for unicode fonts as well as for 8bit fonts.
The table layout can be adjusted in various ways including restricting the
range of output to show only a portion of a specific font. To quickly produce a
one-off table there is a stand-alone version unicodefont.tex that asks you a
few questions and then generates the table -- somewhat similar to nfssfont.tex
for 8-bit fonts.

%package -n texlive-unifront
Summary:        Give notes a unique front page for every chapter and section
Version:        svn67054
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)

%description -n texlive-unifront
This package can help you format your notes easily and give them a unique front
page for every chapter and section. It calculates your progress and then
displays the progress bar under the title. It also displays a partial table of
contents under every progress bar and only shows the subdirectories of the
current part. To generate this, you can simply enter your current completed
titles with a command that accepts Variable Arguments. Still, that also helps
you review your notes. You can also customise the colour of the bar.

%package -n texlive-unisc
Summary:        Unicode small caps with Lua/XeLaTeX
Version:        svn78632
License:        GPL-3.0-or-later AND GFDL-1.3-or-later
