%description -n texlive-unisc
LaTeX produces small caps with \textsc{text} or {\scshape text}. Neither of
these commands produce small caps in Unicode. If the output text is copied and
pasted somewhere it shows the same characters as used in the input. This
package aims to internally convert all the characters provided to the commands
mentioned above. It assumes that the file using this package is compiled with
Lua/XeLaTeX and a good Unicode font which has the small caps characters, e.g.,
Charis SIL.

%package -n texlive-unitconv
Summary:        Convert a length into one with another unit
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(iftex.sty)
Requires:       tex(luacode.sty)
Requires:       tex(xparse.sty)

%description -n texlive-unitconv
This package defines two macros to convert a value with unit into one with
another unit. Supported are all TeX-related units, and also km and m. The
output can be in scientific notation for large values. The package only works
with LuaLaTeX!

%package -n texlive-units
Summary:        Typeset units
Version:        svn42428
License:        GPL-2.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-units-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-units-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)

%description -n texlive-units
The package is provided as a bundle with the nicefrac package for typing
fractions. Units uses nicefrac in typesetting physical units in a
standard-looking sort of way.

%package -n texlive-unravel
Summary:        Watching TeX digest tokens
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-unravel-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-unravel-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(gtl.sty)

%description -n texlive-unravel
The aim of this LaTeX package is to help debug complicated macros. This is done
by letting the user step through the execution of some TeX code, going through
the details of nested expansions, performing assignments, as well as some
simple typesetting commands. To use this package, one should normally run TeX
in a terminal. The unravel package requires up-to-date versions of the
l3kernel, l3packages and l3experimental bundles.

%package -n texlive-updatemarks
Summary:        Extract and update marks from boxes
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(xparse.sty)

%description -n texlive-updatemarks
This package can help you update marks if you put your title in boxes. You can
use \usepackage[minipage,multicol,tcolorbox]{updatemarks} in the preamble of
your document so that marks in these environments can be found by LaTeX. You
can use \ExtractMarks or \ExtractSplitMarks to save marks, and \UpdateMarks to
reinsert them.

